//
// Regenerated 2 September 2026 from the source material already held in
// pipeline/_data (the 34 examination papers 2017-2026 and the 18 published
// marking schemes that cover 2017-2025):
//
//   * every figure re-cropped from the paper PDFs by locating the graphic
//     blocks inside each question and pulling the edges back off neighbouring
//     prose, so a crop no longer ships half a line of somebody else's question
//   * 350 model answers rewritten - 154 that were empty, 106 that described a
//     method instead of answering, 45 bare letter sequences expanded into the
//     mapping they stand for, 7 lifted verbatim from marking-scheme scaffolding
//     ("Two valid countries"), and 38 that answered a different question
//     entirely
//   * ambiguous source labels disambiguated: before this, Part One Q1 and
//     Part Two Q1 of the same 2017-2019 paper carried an identical label
//
// Answers for 2017-2025 were written against that paper's own marking scheme;
// 2026 has no published scheme, so those were written from the paper itself.
// Where a question depends on the Ordnance Survey map sheet or aerial
// photograph issued with the paper - neither of which is contained in the PDFs
// - the answer states what to look for and how to read it rather than
// inventing a grid reference.

