        "question": "State whether each of the following statements is true or false.\n(a) The hinterland is the area beyond a major town or city.\n(b) A nodal region is a region characterised by poor transport.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "True/false statements about regions:\n\n(a) \"The hinterland is the area beyond a major town or city\" - TRUE. The hinterland refers to the surrounding rural area and distant territories connected to and economically dependent on a major urban center. The hinterland typically refers to areas within the sphere of influence of a town or city, receiving services and connected by trade networks to the urban center.\n\n(b) \"A nodal region is a region characterised by poor transport\" - FALSE. A nodal region is NOT characterized by poor transport; rather, it is a region organized around a central node (usually a major city) with good transportation connections radiating outward. Good transport infrastructure and accessibility are typically FEATURES of nodal regions, enabling interaction between the central node and surrounding areas. Poor transport would actually limit the development of nodal regions.",
