        "label": "8B",
        "question": "Examine the development of one of the following with reference to a developed economy that you have studied: Footloose industries, Financial services, Mass tourism.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "Consider the development of mass tourism in Spain as a developed economy with significant economic impacts:\n\nSpain transformed from a relatively poor agrarian economy in the 1960s to a major tourism destination. Tourism now accounts for over 5% of GDP and employs approximately 500,000 people directly. The Balearic and Canary Islands exemplify this development.\n\nThe development involved infrastructure investment including airport construction at Palma de Mallorca and Barcelona-El Prat, hotel development along Mediterranean coasts, and transportation networks. Spanish airline development (Iberia) and European low-cost carriers (Ryanair, EasyJet) provided affordable access.\n\nMarketing campaigns promoted Spain's Mediterranean climate, cultural heritage (Sagrada Familia, Alhambra), and beaches to Northern European markets. The cost differential between Northern Europe and Spain made holidays economically accessible to middle-class families.\n\nEconomic impacts include employment generation in hospitality, construction, and transportation sectors. Local economies in tourism regions experienced significant growth. However, mass tourism also created challenges including environmental degradation of coastlines, cultural impacts on local communities, and seasonal employment instability.",
