        "question": "Using graph paper, draw a suitable graph to illustrate this data.",
        "marks": 10,
        "model": "A suitable graph for this data is a pie chart, because the six figures are percentage shares of a single total — 100% of asylum applications to the European Union in 2021. A bar chart would also be accepted.\n\nHow to draw the pie chart on graph paper:\n• Title it 'Asylum Applications to the European Union in 2021'.\n• Draw a circle with a compass and mark the centre.\n• Convert each percentage to degrees by multiplying by 3.6:\n  Germany 30% → 108°\n  Rest of EU 27% → 97.2°\n  France 19% → 68.4°\n  Spain 10% → 36°\n  Italy 8% → 28.8°\n  Austria 6% → 21.6°\n  (These total 360°.)\n• Draw a radius vertically from the centre to the top of the circle, then measure each angle in turn with a protractor, working clockwise and starting with the largest segment.\n• Shade each segment differently and add a key naming each country and its percentage.\n\nIf a bar chart is drawn instead, put the countries on the horizontal axis, the percentage of all applications on the vertical axis scaled from 0 to 30 in steps of 5, and draw six bars of equal width separated by equal gaps.\n\nMarks are awarded for the title, for accurate conversion and measurement of each segment (or accurate plotting of each bar), and for a key.",
        "diagram": "",
