        "question": "Examine the 1:50 000 Ordnance Survey map and legend accompanying this paper. Imagine you have been given the task of finding a suitable location for a new large hotel within the area covered by the map: (i) State, using a six-figure grid reference, where you would locate the hotel; (ii) Explain the reasons why you chose this location; (iii) Describe one disadvantage of locating the hotel at this location.",
        "marks": 40,
        "model": "Worked Method for Locating a Hotel on Ordnance Survey Map:\n\n(i) Six-Figure Grid Reference for Hotel Location:\n\nThe candidate must examine the provided 1:50 000 Ordnance Survey map and select an appropriate location for a large hotel. A suitable example location might be stated as a six-figure grid reference such as W 265 690 (or another appropriate reference visible on the map). The reference should correspond to an identified suitable location.\n\n(ii) Reasons for Location Choice:\n\nAccessibility and Transportation:\n- Proximity to major road networks (A-roads or motorways shown on the map) for easy access by guests and supply deliveries\n- Proximity to railway stations or public transport connections enabling guest accessibility\n- Distance from congested urban areas while maintaining access to main transportation routes\n\nProximity to Attractions:\n- Location near major tourist attractions, historical sites, or recreational facilities marked on the map\n- Access to natural features (rivers, coastlines, mountains) that attract tourists\n- Distance from industrial areas or less appealing environments\n\nUtilities and Services:\n- Availability of essential services shown on map including water supply, electricity, and sewage systems\n- Proximity to towns or service centres providing banking, medical services, and supply facilities\n- Road access to major urban centres for staff recruitment and guest services\n\nLand Characteristics:\n- Suitable terrain for hotel construction (relatively flat land preferable to steep slopes)\n- Adequate space for building, parking facilities, and potential expansion\n- Avoiding areas prone to flooding or environmental hazards\n\nMarket Considerations:\n- Location in regions with established tourism infrastructure and patterns\n- Proximity to business districts for business travellers (if applicable)\n\n(iii) One Disadvantage of the Chosen Location:\n\nEnvironmental Impact: Development of a large hotel may result in habitat destruction or environmental degradation. Construction and operation increase traffic congestion and associated pollution. Water usage for hotel operations may strain local water resources. Increased waste generation requires adequate disposal facilities. The built structure may visually impact landscapes, particularly in areas of natural beauty or heritage significance.",
