        "label": "A(v)",
        "question": "Name one specific European Union policy which influences the development of agriculture.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "One specific European Union policy influencing agricultural development is the Common Agricultural Policy (CAP). The CAP, established 1962 and reformed multiple times (1992, 2003, 2021 reform), provides direct payments to farmers based on land holding and historical production, guaranteed minimum prices for certain commodities (dairy, beef, cereals), and market regulation mechanisms (quotas limiting production, intervention buying supporting prices when market prices fall). CAP transfers approximately EUR 40 billion annually (40% of EU budget) to agricultural sector, making it single largest EU expenditure. CAP directly impacts agricultural development: production support incentivises intensification (increasing yield per hectare through fertiliser, mechanisation, pesticides), enabling EU farmers to maintain competitiveness despite higher labour costs than developing countries; price guarantees reduce market risk, enabling investment in equipment and buildings; and land payments support farm incomes, particularly for small farms that couldn't compete on market prices alone. However, recent CAP reforms (2021 onwards) introduce environmental conditions (greening requirements, organic farming support) shifting from pure production support toward sustainability objectives.",
