        "label": "A(vii)",
        "question": "Explain briefly one benefit of a region having large numbers of people who have third level education.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "One benefit of a region having large numbers of people with third level education is enhanced economic competitiveness: university-educated workforce (bachelor's degree or higher) earns 40-80% higher lifetime incomes than secondary-educated workers and shows greater adaptability to economic change. Regions with 40%+ tertiary education rates (Ireland's 58.4% in 2020, Netherlands 52.3%) attract knowledge-based industries (software, biotechnology, finance, research) that create high-wage employment. For example, Dublin's concentration of multinational tech headquarters (Google, Facebook, Airbnb) directly reflects Ireland's high tertiary education rates, enabling companies to recruit engineers and specialists locally, reducing recruitment costs and facilitating innovation through clustering of educated workforce. This creates productivity gains and tax revenue exceeding 15-20% in regions with high education levels.",
