        "label": "A(vi)",
        "question": "Life expectancy and mean years of schooling are two factors used to calculate the Human Development Index. Name a third factor.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "A third factor used to calculate the Human Development Index is Gross National Income (GNI) per capita, measured in purchasing power parity (PPP) terms. This measures standard of living and economic productivity, complementing life expectancy (health) and mean years of schooling (education) to create comprehensive development measure capturing three dimensions: long and healthy life, knowledge/education, and decent standard of living.",
