        "question": "Draw an outline map of a European region (not in Ireland) that you have studied. On it, show and name each of the following:\n• Two named urban centres\n• The course of one named river\n• The outline of one named feature of relief (upland or lowland).",
        "marks": 20,
        "model": "To produce a full-marks answer, you must draw a sketch outline map to half scale with dimensions of 12cm x 9cm (allow up to 0.5cm variation). Obtain a standard map of your chosen European region (e.g. the Iberian Peninsula, the Alps, the Danube Basin, or Southern France) and use graph paper to transfer the outline by reducing all linear dimensions to half their original size. The outline must have four clearly drawn sides; do not trace or photocopy the original map. Once the outline is complete, identify and locate two named urban centres on your sketch—for example, Madrid and Barcelona in Spain, or Munich and Hamburg in Germany—and mark these with a clear dot and precise label. Next, draw the course of one named river across the map with a continuous line, tracing from source to mouth or confluence—for example, the Rhine flowing from south to north through Germany, or the Danube following its course through central Europe. Finally, identify one named relief feature (either upland or lowland) and show its outline clearly; examples include the Pyrenees (upland), the North European Plain (lowland), or the Carpathian Mountains. Label all four elements directly on the sketch or in a separate key. Ensure all labelling is legible and placed close to its corresponding feature. The sketch must be drawn on graph paper or in your answer book with a ruler for straight edges. To earn full marks: the outline must be accurately drawn to half scale (4 marks for sketch outline); each of the four features must be shown correctly (3 marks each for showing = 12 marks total) and labelled (1 mark each = 4 marks total). Total: 20 marks.",
