        "question": "Match each of the letters A, B, C and D with the feature that best matches it in the table below.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Volcanoes and earthquakes are distinct natural hazards associated with plate tectonic activity. Volcanoes occur where molten rock (magma) beneath Earth's crust is forced to the surface, erupting lava, ash, and gases. Earthquakes occur when stress accumulated along plate boundaries is suddenly released through rock fracture and movement.\n\nThe features of these hazards can be distinguished as follows:\n- Volcano type A refers to shield volcanoes, which have gentle slopes and are formed by low-viscosity basaltic lava flowing great distances before cooling; examples include Mauna Loa in Hawaii.\n- Volcano type B refers to stratovolcanoes (also called composite volcanoes), which have steep slopes and are formed by alternating layers of lava and pyroclastic material; examples include Mount Vesuvius in Italy and Mount Fuji in Japan.\n- Volcano type C refers to cinder cones, which are small volcanic features formed by explosive eruptions of pyroclastic material.\n- Earthquake feature D refers to the epicenter, which is the point on Earth's surface directly above the focus (the point within the crust where an earthquake originates).",
