        "label": "(ii)",
        "question": "Name one example of an active volcano.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "One example of an active volcano is Mount Sakurajima in Japan. Mount Sakurajima is located in Kyushu in southern Japan and is one of the world's most active volcanoes, erupting continuously for many decades. It is situated at the junction of the Philippine, Eurasian, and North American tectonic plates, making it an area of intense volcanic activity. The volcano has produced frequent small to moderate eruptions, ejecting ash and volcanic gases regularly. These eruptions affect the surrounding communities, particularly the city of Kagoshima nearby, which experiences regular ashfall. Sakurajima's volcanic activity demonstrates the hazards associated with living in volcanically active regions and the importance of volcanic monitoring and hazard management systems in areas of persistent volcanic activity.",
