        "label": "A(iv)",
        "question": "How many times has river rejuvenation taken place in the diagram above?",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "The number of rejuvenation episodes in river valleys is determined by counting the number of distinct knickpoints, terraces, or major gradient changes visible on the river profile diagram. Each terrace level represents one complete cycle of incision followed by stability. Diagrams showing multiple past sea level positions indicate multiple rejuvenation episodes - typically one rejuvenation occurred for each significant sea level change. For the section shown, if two knickpoints are visible, rejuvenation has occurred twice, indicating the river has experienced two periods of renewed erosive activity separated by an interval of stability. The number corresponds to discrete lowerings of base level recorded in the river morphology.",
        "diagram": "",
