        "label": "A(iii)",
        "question": "Explain briefly what is meant by the term lithification.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Lithification is the process by which unconsolidated sediment transforms into solid sedimentary rock through compaction and cementation. As overlying sediment layers accumulate weight from successive deposits, lower sediment beds experience progressive pressure and temperature increases. Compaction removes water and air from sediment pores as grains are pressed together. Cementation occurs when mineral-rich groundwater percolates through sediment and deposits mineral cement between grains, bonding them together. Common cements include silica, calcite, and iron oxide. The combination of compaction and cementation lithifies loose sediment into resistant rock over geological timescales.",
        "diagram": "",
        "source_page": 18,
        "model_source": "ai-h1"
