        "question": "Examine the 1:50 000 Ordnance Survey map and legend accompanying this paper. Draw a sketch map of the area shown to half scale. On it, correctly show and label each of the following: The built up area of Macroom, The entire route of the R584 road, The entire route of the N22 road, An electricity transmission line.",
        "marks": 20,
        "model": "**Worked Method**: To complete this sketch map: (1) Using the 1:50,000 OS map provided, measure the map dimensions and draw the outline to half scale (approximately 12cm × 9cm as specified in marking criteria). (2) Carefully identify Macroom's built-up area (shown in urban shading on the map) and sketch this boundary at half scale, labelling it. (3) Trace the complete R584 road route from start to finish across the map, marking all sections including curves and junctions, then label. (4) Similarly, trace the full N22 road route showing all its extent on the map and label appropriately. (5) Identify electricity transmission lines (shown as crossed circles or dashed lines in the map legend) and sketch their complete route across the map area, labelling as 'Electricity transmission line'. Ensure all features are shown with accuracy and correctly labelled. The sketch demonstrates understanding of settlement distribution, transport infrastructure, and utility provision in the landscape.",
