        "question": "Name two barriers to migration.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "Two barriers to migration are financial constraints and language barriers. Financial constraints include the cost of transport, visa fees, accommodation deposits, and initial living expenses—prohibitive for many potential migrants from lower-income countries, limiting migration to wealthy individuals. Language barriers create difficulties in communication, employment prospects, and social integration—migrants unable to speak the destination country's language face employment discrimination, limited job options outside low-skilled roles, and social isolation, discouraging migration. Other examples include immigration restrictions and cultural differences.",
