        "model": "Agriculture represents a primary economic activity significantly contributing to Brazil's national economy. Brazil produces and exports vast quantities of agricultural products: soybeans (world's largest exporter at 40+ million tonnes annually, primarily from Mato Grosso); coffee (25% of global production); sugarcane (90% of sugar and ethanol exports); beef (world's largest exporter at 10+ million tonnes annually); and oranges (world's largest juice exporter). These commodities generate billions in export revenue annually, supporting rural economies from the Amazon frontier to the southern plateaus. Agricultural technology advancement (no-till farming, precision agriculture using GPS and drones) increased productivity significantly. Agribusiness enterprises process and export these products globally, representing secondary activity as well.",
