        "model": "Answer with reference to the Indian sub-continent (a Continental / Sub-Continental region, not in Europe).\n\nDraw a freehand outline of the sub-continent about a quarter of a page in size — the triangular peninsula with the Arabian Sea to the west, the Bay of Bengal to the east and the Himalayan wall across the north. Then show and name each of the three required items, each earning marks separately for showing and for naming:\n\n• Two named urban centres — Mumbai, marked with a dot on the west coast, and Delhi, marked in the north on the Ganges Plain, both labelled. (Kolkata, Chennai and Bangalore are equally acceptable.)\n• The course of a named river — the Ganges, drawn from the Himalayas eastwards across the Northern Plains to its delta on the Bay of Bengal, and labelled. (The Indus or the Brahmaputra would serve equally.)\n• The outline of a named feature of relief — the Himalayas, outlined as a band across the northern edge of the region and labelled. (The Deccan Plateau as an upland, or the Northern Plains as a lowland, would serve equally.)\n\nDo not draw a European or Irish region. Names may be written on the map or set out in a key; a feature shown without a name scores nothing for showing, but a correct name still earns its mark where the location is inaccurate.",
