        "model": "Carbonation. Rainwater absorbs carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and from the soil to form a weak carbonic acid. When this weak acid soaks into limestone it reacts with the calcium carbonate of the rock and converts it to calcium bicarbonate, which is soluble and is carried away in solution. The acid works fastest along the bedding planes and joints, widening them into grikes at the surface and into caves underground.",
