        "model": "Candidates must identify two renewable energy sources suitable for the mapped area and provide location evidence using grid references or notation visible on the OS map or aerial photograph.\n\nMETHODOLOGY: From the OS map or aerial photograph, identify terrain features suggesting renewable energy viability. Wind turbines require exposed locations with consistent wind exposure; identify elevated areas, exposed ridges, or coastal locations. Solar installations require unshaded south-facing slopes or open ground. Hydropower requires flowing water with elevation changes; identify watercourses with steep gradients. Biomass requires agricultural or forestry resources; identify fields, forests, or agricultural land use.\n\nEXAMPLE ANSWERS: (1) Wind power at grid reference [identify elevated area from map]—this location receives consistent Atlantic/prevailing winds, has exposed terrain without obstruction, and proximity to the electrical grid for transmission. (2) Hydropower at grid reference [identify river with steep gradient]—this river shows elevation changes suitable for developing hydroelectric potential; flowing water and gravitational head enable power generation.\n\nMARKING: 2 marks for naming renewable energy source, 2 marks for grid reference/location. Total: 4 marks per energy source. Accurate location evidence from map features is essential.",
