        "marks": 10,
        "model": "With reference to one renewable energy source named in part (i), explain the advantages of the chosen location (7 marks):\n\nEXAMPLE—WIND POWER AT [GRID REFERENCE]: This location provides several advantages: (1) Exposure—elevation and lack of surrounding obstacles permit consistent wind flow unimpeded by terrain or vegetation, maximising energy generation. (2) Wind resource—the location receives Atlantic or prevailing winds characteristic of the marine region, providing reliable, consistent wind speeds exceeding minimum thresholds (typically 7+ m/s) for economical turbine operation. (3) Grid proximity—proximity to existing electrical transmission infrastructure permits connection to national grid without excessive cable costs. (4) Minimal disruption—the location is sparsely populated, avoiding residential areas where noise and visual impact create opposition. (5) Distance from aviation—clearance from airspace ensures aviation safety. (6) Transportation access—road access facilitates turbine installation and maintenance. These factors combine to make this location optimal for wind power development.",
