        "model": "Explain one reason why local people might object to this renewable energy development (4 marks):\n\nLOCAL OPPOSITION EXAMPLES: (1) Visual impact—wind turbines are large visible structures (80+ metres high) that dominate landscapes, particularly in areas valued for aesthetic beauty or tourism. Local communities may oppose the visual intrusion on cherished landscapes. (2) Noise pollution—operating wind turbines generate noise (35-45 decibels at typical distances), affecting nearby residents' quality of life, particularly during night hours. (3) Wildlife impact—wind turbines kill birds and bats colliding with blades, affecting endangered species. (4) Property values—proximity to wind farms reportedly reduces nearby property values by 5-10%, affecting landowners financially. (5) Agricultural disruption—wind farm development requires land acquisition, removing productive agricultural land. These represent genuine concerns legitimate communities raise regarding renewable energy development, even when supporting climate action generally.",
