        "label": "A",
        "question": "Examine the table above about Ireland's largest towns in 2011, 2016 and 2022, and answer each of the following questions: (i) What was Ireland's largest town in 2022?; (ii) What was the population of Swords in 2016?; (iii) Which town had a population of less than 30,000 in 2011?; (iv) Calculate the growth in Dundalk's population from 2011 to 2022; (v) Explain briefly one possible reason for the growth in population of the towns in the table above; (vi) Explain briefly one impact of the growth in population of these towns.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "(i) IRELAND'S LARGEST TOWN IN 2022: Drogheda was Ireland's largest town in 2022 with a population of 44,135, representing the highest population figure in the provided table.\n\n(ii) SWORDS POPULATION IN 2016: Swords had a population of 39,248 in 2016, showing steady growth from 36,924 in 2011 toward 40,776 in 2022.\n\n(iii) TOWN WITH POPULATION LESS THAN 30,000 IN 2011: Navan had a population of 28,559 in 2011, the only town in the table below 30,000 in that year. The data shows Navan grew to 30,173 (2016) and 33,886 (2022), reflecting sustained expansion.\n\n(iv) GROWTH IN DUNDALK'S POPULATION 2011-2022: Dundalk's population grew from 37,816 (2011) to 43,112 (2022), representing an increase of 5,296 people over the 11-year period, demonstrating significant expansion.\n\n(v) REASON FOR TOWN GROWTH: One significant reason for these towns' population growth is economic development and employment creation. Dublin's spatial expansion through commuter-belt growth has extended northward along transport corridors; Drogheda, Dundalk, Swords and other towns in this table have attracted multinational manufacturing, technology sector employment (particularly in Swords near Dublin), and retail services establishing distribution centers for national operations. These employment opportunities attract rural migrants and young professionals seeking career advancement unavailable in smaller settlements, driving sustained urban population increase.\n\n(vi) IMPACT OF TOWN GROWTH: One significant impact of population growth in these towns is housing demand and infrastructure strain. Rapid population increases outpace residential construction capacity, increasing property prices and rental costs, pricing out low-income households and reducing housing affordability. Infrastructure systems including water supply, sewerage treatment, electricity distribution, and road networks designed for smaller populations face demand exceeding capacity during peak usage periods. Educational facility shortages emerge as school enrollment increases faster than school construction; healthcare facility pressures intensify as population-to-GP ratios worsen and hospital waiting times increase. However, growth also generates tax revenue enabling infrastructure investment and business expansion.",
