        "question": "Explain briefly the term compression as it relates to folding.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "Compression, as it relates to folding, is the pushing together or squeezing of rock layers by tectonic forces. Compression occurs when adjacent lithospheric plates collide—continental plates moving toward each other apply horizontal compressional stress to intervening rocks. Layers of rock respond to compression by buckling and folding: layers bend upward forming anticlines and downward forming synclines. Compression is the primary force causing rock deformation in fold mountain building.",
