        "question": "Name two types of fault.",
        "marks": 1,
        "model": "Two types of fault are normal faults and reverse faults. Normal faults form where rocks are pulled apart (tensile stress); the hanging wall (overlying rock) slides down relative to the footwall (underlying rock), creating a depression or graben. Reverse faults form where rocks are pushed together (compressional stress); the hanging wall slides up relative to the footwall, creating elevated features.",
