        "question": "Name two landscape features formed by faulting.",
        "marks": 1,
        "model": "Two landscape features formed by faulting are: (1) rift valleys—depressions created by normal faults where central block subsides between two parallel faults, as seen in the East African Rift Valley; (2) fault scarps or fault lines—abrupt changes in elevation marking fault planes where rock displacement creates visible cliffs or ridges. Other examples include grabens (depressed blocks) and horsts (elevated blocks).",
        "diagram": "",
