        "marks": 20,
        "model": "**Worked Method**: Draw outline map of a continental region (e.g., West Africa, East Africa, Southeast Asia, South America) you have studied. Show: (1) Map outline—country or region boundaries clearly drawn to recognizable proportions (approximately 9-12cm). (2) Named river—identify major river system (e.g., Niger, Congo, Amazon, Mekong) showing complete course from source toward mouth/delta; label river name. (3) Feature of relief—outline area of major topographic feature: mountain range (e.g., Atlas Mountains, Andes), highlands (e.g., East African highlands), or lowland basin (e.g., Congo Basin); label clearly indicating feature name and whether upland or lowland. (4) Two urban centers—mark city locations with symbols; label each city name ensuring they are actually in the studied region (not invented). Examples: Accra and Kumasi (West Africa), Nairobi and Mombasa (East Africa). Accuracy of geographic positioning and correct naming are essential. The outline demonstrates geographic understanding of regional structure.",
