        "model": "One significant challenge facing multinational companies located in Ireland is rising labor costs and wage pressures. As the Irish economy recovers and employment increases, wage inflation occurs, particularly in skilled sectors. Competition for skilled workers among employers drives up salaries and benefits, increasing operational costs for MNCs. This wage cost escalation reduces the competitive cost advantage that Ireland once possessed as a location for MNC investment compared to other European countries or alternative low-cost manufacturing locations, potentially leading some companies to consider relocating operations to regions with lower labor costs or to reconsider expansion plans in Ireland.",
