        "label": "A(v)",
        "question": "Name two indicators used to calculate a country's Human Development Index.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "The Human Development Index is calculated using two main indicators (alongside others): life expectancy at birth, which measures health and longevity outcomes, and mean years of schooling/expected years of schooling, which measure educational attainment. A third indicator is Gross National Income per capita, which reflects economic wealth and living standards. These three dimensions—health, education, and income—combine to create a comprehensive measure of human development beyond simple economic metrics.",
        "diagram": "exam-images/geography/2020-HL-Q9-A-v.png",
