        "marks": 20,
        "model": "A sketch map of the aerial photograph drawn at half scale (approximately 13.9cm by 9.1cm) would accurately represent four key features. The river would be depicted as a curving watercourse, shown with wavy or parallel lines to indicate flowing water, tracing its path through the landscape from upstream toward downstream direction visible in the photograph. The bridge would be precisely located where the river is crossed, marked with an appropriate symbol (line or rectangle perpendicular to the river) and labelled to indicate this infrastructure feature connecting areas separated by the river. The running track in the middleground would be shown as an oval or rectangular circuit, depicted with concentric oval lines or boundary marking to indicate the athletic facility's form, positioned in the middle distance of the sketch as visible in the aerial photograph. The lake in the left foreground would be represented as a defined water body, drawn with appropriate water symbols (shading, blue colouring, or water-specific hatching) and positioned in the left portion of the sketch in the foreground area. All four features must be accurately positioned relative to each other, maintaining proportions and spatial relationships visible in the original aerial photograph, with clear labels either on the sketch features themselves or in an accompanying legend. The sketch outline must be drawn with four complete sides at half scale, representing the photographic area correctly reduced.",
