        "question": "Using graph paper, draw a suitable graph to illustrate this data.",
        "marks": 10,
        "model": "A suitable graph for this data is a pie chart, because the six figures are percentage shares of a single total — 100% of asylum applications to Ireland in the first nine months of 2019. A bar chart would also be accepted.\n\nHow to draw the pie chart on graph paper:\n• Title it 'Nationality of Asylum Seekers in Ireland, first nine months of 2019'.\n• Draw a circle with a compass and mark the centre.\n• Convert each percentage to degrees by multiplying by 3.6:\n  Other 40% → 144°\n  Albania 23% → 82.8°\n  Georgia 15% → 54°\n  Zimbabwe 8% → 28.8°\n  South Africa 7% → 25.2°\n  Nigeria 7% → 25.2°\n  (These total 360°.)\n• Draw a radius vertically from the centre to the top of the circle, then measure each angle in turn with a protractor, working clockwise and starting with the largest segment.\n• Shade each segment differently and add a key naming each nationality and its percentage.\n\nIf a bar chart is drawn instead, put the nationalities on the horizontal axis, the percentage of total applications on the vertical axis scaled from 0 to 40 in steps of 5, and draw six bars of equal width separated by equal gaps.\n\nMarks are awarded for the title, for accurate conversion and measurement of each segment (or for accurate plotting of each bar), and for a key.",
        "diagram": "exam-images/geography/2020-HL-Q12-A-i.png",
