        "model": "One significant impact of Ireland having a large number of retired people is increased demand for healthcare and social care services. The elderly population requires more frequent medical visits, prescription medications, hospitalisation and long-term care (nursing homes, home care services). This increases healthcare system costs and requires substantial government expenditure on pensions and elderly care. Ireland's ageing population (currently 14% over 65; projected to increase to 28% by 2050) creates growing budgetary pressure. Additionally, large retired populations reduce the working-age population supporting pensions through taxes; fewer workers must support more retirees, potentially requiring increased tax rates or reduced pension benefits. Elderly populations also increase housing demand for accessible, age-friendly accommodation and care facilities, creating infrastructure challenges. However, retired people also contribute economically through consumer spending and tourism, providing some offsetting benefits.",
