        "label": "(iii)",
        "question": "State what is meant by the term permeable rock.",
        "marks": 3,
        "model": "PERMEABLE ROCK DEFINITION: Permeable rock is rock with the capacity to allow water to pass through it due to interconnected pores or fissures within the rock structure. Permeable rocks like sandstone, chalk, and limestone have numerous small spaces (pores) between mineral grains that enable water infiltration and groundwater flow. Water permeability is essential for groundwater storage and movement through aquifers. Permeability contrasts with impermeable rock (like granite or clay) which blocks water passage due to dense composition and absent interconnected pore spaces. The degree of rock permeability determines water availability for groundwater resources and affects landscape development through infiltration-dependent erosion processes.",
