        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Two fishing ports in Ireland:\n\n1. **Howth** (County Dublin): A major fishing port on the Dublin coast serving the Irish and European fishing fleets. Howth harbor accommodates fishing vessels and commercial shipping, with fish processing facilities and seafood export infrastructure.\n\n2. **Dingle** (County Kerry): A significant fishing port in southwest Ireland serving local fishing communities and landing catches of white fish and shellfish. Dingle is known for traditional fishing heritage and lobster/crab fishing.",
