        "question": "Explain briefly one advantage of fishing to the Irish economy.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "One advantage of fishing to the Irish economy: **Employment and Rural Development**.\n\nFishing provides direct employment for approximately 16,000 fishermen and indirect employment in processing, distribution, and hospitality sectors (estimated 30,000+ jobs total). Fishing income sustains rural coastal communities (Donegal, Kerry, Cork, Galway) where alternative employment opportunities are limited. Export of Irish seafood generates €700+ million in annual revenue, making it a significant export sector. Communities dependent on fishing maintain population and economic activity: without fishing income, many coastal villages would experience depopulation and economic decline.",
