        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Mantle – D\nVolcanic activity – C\nSubducting plate – B\nContinental plate – A\n\nThe diagram shows a destructive plate boundary: the denser oceanic plate (B) is being forced down beneath the lighter continental plate (A) into the mantle (D), and the magma generated above the descending slab rises to produce volcanic activity (C) at the surface.",
        "diagram": "exam-images/geography/2024-OL-Q1-i.png",
