        "label": "C",
        "question": "(i) Name one developing economy which has been colonised.\n(ii) Explain the impacts of colonialism on this developing economy.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "(i) Nigeria represents a developing economy subject to colonial rule by Britain until 1960. (ii) Colonialism created profound impacts on Nigeria: Economic structures created were extractive, focused on primary commodity exports (oil, minerals, agricultural products) rather than developing diversified economies. Colonial powers controlled natural resources and profits, limiting local capital accumulation for development. Infrastructure investment was restricted to colonial administrative needs and export industries rather than benefiting local populations. Political institutions transplanted from colonial powers lacked local legitimacy and adaptation to indigenous governance systems. Education systems prioritized colonial language and colonial administrative training rather than technical skills needed for development. Colonial boundaries divided ethnic groups and united others, creating ongoing ethnic tensions and political conflicts. Social hierarchies placing colonial Europeans above local populations created lasting inequalities. Institutional weakness persisting after independence created governance challenges. Dependency relationships with former colonial powers limited policy autonomy. These interconnected colonial legacies continue constraining development decades after independence.",
