        "question": "(i) Using graph paper, draw a suitable graph to illustrate this data.\n(ii) In your answer book, state two ways that life expectancy could be increased in countries such as Mali and Sudan.",
        "marks": 30,
        "model": "**Worked Method for Graphs and Statements**: (1) Draw a suitable graph on graph paper (3 marks): Select bar chart, pie chart, or line graph. Vertical axis should be labeled with the variable (e.g., 'Life Expectancy (years)') and appropriate scale (0-80 years for Mali/Sudan data). Horizontal axis labeled with countries. Five data items plotted accurately for each region. (2) Two ways to increase life expectancy in Mali and Sudan (6 marks): First way—improve healthcare infrastructure: Expanded clinics, hospitals, and maternal healthcare reduce infant and child mortality (currently 10+ per 1000 live births). Healthcare training increases doctor and nurse availability, reducing preventable deaths from malaria, tuberculosis, HIV/AIDS. Vaccination programs eliminate infectious diseases; antibiotics and modern medicines extend survival. Clean water and sanitation systems reduce waterborne disease deaths. Second way—improve education, particularly female education: Educated women practice better nutrition, childcare, and birth spacing, reducing child mortality. Female education improves health literacy; women with secondary education have children with higher survival rates. Education reduces fertility, enabling women to space births, improving maternal and child health. Combined, these interventions directly extend life expectancy by reducing premature deaths.",
