        "model": "Overtourism creates significant problems in developed economies like Switzerland. Mountain hiking trails and Alpine resorts experience visitor congestion degrading the natural environment and reducing visitor experience quality. Popular ski resorts face overcrowding during peak season (December-February), creating long lift queues and crowded slopes. Increased traffic congestion in mountain valleys and towns creates air pollution, noise, and infrastructure strain. Water consumption by resort hotels and restaurants stresses local water supplies in Alpine communities. Waste generation from tourism (food, packaging, sewage) exceeds local treatment capacity, causing environmental degradation. Rising real estate values driven by tourism investment make housing unaffordable for local workers, causing community disruption and resident displacement. Traditional communities lose cultural identity as tourism commercializes local culture and transforms villages into tourist attractions.",
