        "question": "Using graph paper, draw a suitable graph to illustrate this data.",
        "marks": 15,
        "model": "A suitable graph for traffic congestion data would be a bar chart with cities (Dublin, London, Lisbon, Copenhagen, Madrid) on the horizontal axis and congestion level (%) on the vertical axis. The vertical axis should range from 0 to 40 percent. Each city is represented by a vertical bar with height proportional to its congestion percentage. Dublin bar reaches 38%, London reaches 31%, Lisbon reaches 23%, Copenhagen reaches 18%, and Madrid reaches 15%. All five cities are accurately plotted and clearly labelled.",
