        "question": "Examine the 1:50 000 Ordnance Survey map and legend accompanying this paper. Draw a sketch map of the area shown to half scale. On it, correctly show and label each of the following: The entire area of Lough Cullin, The course of the River Moy between G 259 024 and G 269 090, Mark an X at the confluence of the River Moy and the Yellow River, The entire area of land above 200 metres.",
        "marks": 20,
        "model": "To complete this 1:50,000 OS map sketch map task successfully, work at precisely half scale (target 12cm × 9cm). Draw a clear four-sided frame to define your sketch boundaries. Locate Lough Cullin on the source map and show its entire water area with accurate positioning. Find the River Moy between the specified grid references (G 259 024 to G 269 090) and trace its complete course, showing bends and flow direction. Mark an X precisely at the river confluence point where the Moy meets the Yellow River by examining map symbols for river junctions. Finally, identify contour lines exceeding 200 metres elevation and shade or pattern the entire upland area above this height. Label each feature clearly either on the map itself or in a key. Accuracy of location and proportion matters significantly—use gridlines to maintain relative positions. The sketch outline earns 4 marks for correct proportions and impressions; each of the four features earns 3 marks for showing and 1 mark for labelling, for a total of 20 marks.",
        "diagram": "",
